## Tile rule

A verified JITA number (same authority as r518: `validated-navision-import-v1`, identity verified, column present, a digit, not all zeros) paints the whole Parts station green only when there is no imported parts status, or that status is green. Orange, red, review and grey keep their colour. The JITA mark is the existing bottom-right corner tick (`.has-jita`). A parts stoppage stays a stoppage. `public.pdc_jita_eta` is not read.

`styles.css` is unchanged. The imported-colour classes and the corner mark were already there. Department 135 / Karratha is frozen: `karratha/app.js` is not edited, and root `styles.css` stays byte-identical to the Karratha copy. Cache bust `r524=2026.10.24.r524` on `app.js` and `sales/pmb-stations.js` only.

## Should r518 stop setting parts_received?

The tile bug is the frontend short-circuit. Clearing `vehicle_parts_updates.parts_received` does not by itself change the tile, because the short-circuit keys off the JITA number. Go-live ships the tile fix and leaves the data change unapplied.

What the stored tick changes, beyond the tile, for those 118:

- The board mapper sets `pdcCompleteParts` from `parts_update.parts_received` after the PARTS work item. Both are true today, so PARTS counts as signed off in completed-jobs text, vehicle search, the CSV export, and the note written when a vehicle is transferred to RFT.
- `refreshSharedVehicleWorkState` reads the parts row and forces the parts work state to complete when `parts_received` is true.
- `pdc-parts-confirmation.js` already replaces `partsStateComplete` for a `separate_parts_status` feed with the import's `parts_complete`. Parts queue filters that use that wrapper already follow the import, so they do not hide these 118. The tile was the surface that ignored the import.
- `parts_ordered`, `worst_eta`, parts stoppage, the email Parts ETA, `set_parts_eta` and `pdc_jita_eta` are not written by the tick and would stay as they are.
- None of the 118 are at a QC or RFT location, so applying the option would not reopen a QC gate. A later RFT transfer note would stop listing PARTS as signed off. Each cleared work item still fires the QC operation-lines cache invalidation, and deleting the parts row bumps the email vehicle revision.
- The tick runs when a current Navision row is saved, not when the parts importer runs. Importers are unchanged. Changing only the function would not untick the 118, because the function returns immediately when the station is already received. A vehicle that is green, gets ticked, and later turns orange stays ticked for the same reason. The data script and the function change have to travel together if the stored tick is to match the tile.

The option, not applied:

`supabase/proposals/r524_jita_outstanding_parts_option.sql`

- file md5 `23e146353c475135a2f1b6709038784e`
- new `tick_parts_jita_from_navision_518` prosrc md5 `1e6833c19f876a1abddb3c26aa90a2aa`

`supabase/proposals/r524_jita_outstanding_parts_option.down.sql`

- file md5 `3ef3ef874123d1648da2c989239dc2a5`
- restored prosrc md5 `d39a7051efd9669c6eda97437150feab` (the live r518 body)

It is not under `supabase/migrations`, so a deploy will not run it. It refuses unless the clock second is 02–45, the staging sentinel is `cdsmnqxtyyoeoznmbidd`, and the production sentinel is absent. It must be one transaction. It refuses unless the tick, the trigger, `set_parts_eta`, and both parts-flags functions still have their current md5s. It updates the existing r518 pin in place and does not add a pin. The new body still contains `validated-navision-import-v1` and does not contain `pdc_jita_eta`, `worst_eta` or `set_parts_eta`, so `navision_jita_station_tick_518` still passes. Before any write, if `pdc_parts_flags_vehicle_20260911` colour is orange or red, the function returns false and does not untick a station that is already received. Grey and review still tick. An active parts-complete email makes that read green, so those still tick.

The data half inserts `pdc_ops.r524_outstanding_parts_option_audit` (RLS on, revoked from public, anon, authenticated and service_role) for the 118 pristine orange or red inserts, deletes those parts rows, and clears those PARTS work items back to not required and not complete (`pdc_772` blocks deleting a work item). On the 24 Oct read that set is exactly the 118 orange stocks above. The down script puts the parts rows and the work-item completion back, restores the r518 function and pin, and drops the audit table. It refuses if a parts row already exists again for an audited vehicle.

Recommendation: ship the tile fix. Leave this SQL for a later decision. It changes stored station completion, search, CSV and RFT notes, not just the tile.
